t a K or 10, or potentially win with my K high.\n\n**Answer: 0**\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: I possess King-high (K, 10) on a board of 7, 5, 3, 6. The board is coordinated with straight possibilities (any 4 makes a straight) and two hearts. The opponent has shown passivity by checking on the pre-flop, flop, and turn. My hand has some showdown value as high cards, but not enough to value bet confidently. Betting might force out worse hands while getting called by better ones (pairs). Checking back allows me to see the river for free, potentially hitting a King or Ten to improve, or winning at showdown with King-high if the opponent is also weak.\n\nReason: The pot is small, and the board texture is wet (connected). My hand is currently just King-high. Since the opponent checked, taking a free card to try and improve on the river or get to showdown cheaply is the most prudent play.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
