und (Pre-flop, Flop, Turn), which strongly indicates weakness—likely Air, a small pocket pair, or a weak pair like 3x. While you are likely ahead, betting has "thin value"; worse hands will likely fold, and better hands (traps) will call or raise. Since you are currently leading the cumulative game and the pot is small, there is no need to take unnecessary risks. Checking allows you to win the pot if you are ahead without risking chips if the opponent is slow-playing a Queen or better two pair.\n\nReason: Your hand has showdown value but is easily beaten by a Queen, Jack, or higher pocket pair. The opponent\'s passivity suggests a weak hand, so checking gets you to showdown for free to claim the pot if you are best, avoiding the risk of betting into a trap or getting raised.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
