ith a marginal hand. Checking is the most prudent play to realize your hand\'s equity without investing more chips prematurely.\n\nReason: You have a suited connector gap hand (T6s) which plays well if you hit the board but is weak otherwise. Since the opponent did not raise, you can see the flop for free (Check). There is no incentive to raise and build a large pot with a mediocre hand, nor should you fold when you can play for free.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
