lay large pots, and 2) 8d 9d relies on hitting the board to be strong. Seeing the flop for free maximizes the value of this hand without bloating the pot prematurely with just 8-high.\n\nReason: I have a suited connector which has high potential to make a strong hand post-flop, but currently only has 8-high. Since I can see the flop for free (Check), this is the most efficient way to realize the hand\'s equity without risking chips out of position before seeing the community cards.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
